STRUCTURES = [
 ("Isolated Queen's Pawn (IQP)", "r1bq1rk1/pp3ppp/2n1pn2/3p4/3P4/2NB1N2/PP3PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w - - 0 1",
  "White owns the d4 pawn with no c/e neighbours. It cannot be defended by pawns, but gives space and open files. White: attack, piece activity, e4/d5 breaks, avoid queen-side endgames. Black: blockade d5, trade pieces, aim for the endgame where the pawn is weak."),
 ("Carlsbad (Exchange QGD)", "r1bq1rk1/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/3p4/3P4/2NBPN2/PP3PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w - - 0 1",
  "White has e3/d4 against Black's c6/d5/e6. White plays the minority attack (b4-b5) to create a weak c6/c7 pawn. Black counters with ...Ne4, ...f5 or a kingside space gain. Keep the knight on e5 or d2 for activity."),
 ("French Chain", "r1bqkb1r/pp3ppp/2n1pn2/2ppP3/3P4/2P2N2/PP3PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 0 1",
  "The pawn chain e5/d4 versus e6/d5. Attack the base of the chain: Black hits d4 with ...c5, ...Qb6 and ...Nc6; White hits e5's support or goes after the kingside. Remember: base of the pawn chain is the target."),
 ("Open Sicilian (Scheveningen)", "r1bqk2r/1p2bppp/p1nppn2/8/3NPP2/2N1B3/PPP1B1PP/R2QK2R w KQkq - 0 1",
  "White has e4 with a central space edge; Black has the half-open c-file and a flexible d6/e6 setup. Black's plan: ...Qc7, ...b5, ...Bb7 and ...d5 to equalize; White's plan: f4-f5 or g4-g5 for a kingside attack."),
]
